title: "Reproducibility code for Sparse and Gaussian Priors for Weak-Lensing Mass Mapping: Observable-Dependent Performance on FAIR Universe Simulations"
authors:
  - family-names: "de Araujo"
    given-names: "Rafael L."
    affiliation: "Federal University of Bahia"
  - family-names: "Pestana"
    given-names: "Reynam da C."
    affiliation: "Federal University of Bahia"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility code, frozen settings, validation-derived power spectrum,
  compact numerical results, and analysis scripts for the manuscript
  Sparse and Gaussian Priors for Weak-Lensing Mass Mapping:
  Observable-Dependent Performance on FAIR Universe Simulations.
  Authors: Rafael L. de Araujo and Reynam da C. Pestana,
  Federal University of Bahia.
  The package includes the core mass-mapping implementations, comparison
  drivers for MCALens and GLIMPSE, fusion and ADMM audit scripts, and provenance
  for the retained inputs and results. Raw FAIR Universe data are obtained
  separately from https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20056065.
  Validation includes 162 consistency checks against seven manuscript tables
  and a server smoke test of one patch with KS, Starlet, G+S, MCALens and GLIMPSE.
  This does not establish regeneration of all 480 cases, bootstrap samples or
  figures, or installation in a fresh environment.
  License scope: MIT applies to Rafael L. de Araujo's original contributions.
  The bundled GLIMPSE source and its modifications retain CeCILL 2.1;
  CosmoStat/MCALens and the preserved patch retain the CosmoStat MIT license
  and copyright. These third-party components are not relicensed by the root
  MIT license. See LICENSE_SCOPE.md and the included upstream license notices.
keywords:
  - weak gravitational lensing
  - mass mapping
  - reproducibility
